{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":4,"query":"name=Davies&limit=10&title=Editing Humanity","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":[{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":[{"title":"Editing humanity ","subTitle":"the CRISPR revolution and the new era of genome editing "},{"@type":"alternative","title":"CRISPR revolution and the new era of genome editing"}],"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Davies, Kevin,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1960-"}],"role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author"}}],"nameIdentifier":"https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCjDVBCYV6wJCT6BDjrXqkP"},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2020"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2020"},"issuance":"monographic","edition":"First Pegasus Books cloth edition."},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"Pegasus Books,","role":{"roleTerm":"publisher"}},"dateIssued":"2020."}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"xviii, 446 pages, 16 unnumbered pages of plates : illustrations (some color) ; 24 cm"},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"illustration"}},{"form":{"@type":"Color content","#text":"polychrome"}}],"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"If our genes are, to a great extent, our destiny, then what would happen if mankind could engineer and alter the very essence of our DNA coding? Millions might be spared the devastating effects of hereditary disease or the challenges of disability, whether it was the pain of sickle-cell anemia to the ravages of Huntington's disease. But this power to \"play God\" also raises major ethical questions and poses threats for potential misuse. For decades, these questions have lived exclusively in the realm of science fiction, but as Kevin Davies powerfully reveals in his new book, this is all about to change."},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"The CRISPR craze -- A cut above -- We can be heroes -- \"Thelma and Louise\" -- DNA surgery -- Field of dreams -- Prize fight -- Genome editing B.C. -- Deliverance or disaster -- The rise and fall of gene therapy -- Overnight success -- Fix you -- Patent pending -- #CRISPRbabies -- The boy from Xinhua -- Breaking the glass -- A maculate conception -- Crossing the germline -- Going rogue -- To extinction and beyond -- Farm aid -- CRISPR prime -- Volitional evolution -- Bases loaded."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Kevin Davies."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (pages [379]-423) and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"CRISPR (Genetics)"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Gene editing","Moral and ethical aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Genetics","Moral and ethical aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"DNA"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":["Clustered Regularly Interspaced Short Palindromic Repeats","genetics"]},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"DNA"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Édition génique","Aspect moral"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Génétique","Aspect moral"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"ADN"},{"@authority":"fast","@href":"(OCoLC)fst00940130","topic":["Genetics","Moral and ethical aspects"]},{"@authority":"fast","@href":"(OCoLC)fst02000514","topic":"CRISPR (Genetics)"},{"@authority":"fast","@href":"(OCoLC)fst008